\pard\sa80\fs22 These are all Microsoft Configuration Manager (ConfigMgr / SCCM / MECM) parameters. Here's what each does in plain terms:\par
\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Parameter\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 What it is\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 When it's needed\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -Domain\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 The Active Directory domain the server should join after build (e.g. corp.example.com)\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Only for post-build validation - verifying the server joined the domain correctly\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SiteCode\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 A 3-character ConfigMgr site identifier (e.g. P01)\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Only when building a ConfigMgr bootable ISO - tells ConfigMgr which site to associate the media with\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -ManagementPoint\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 The FQDN of the ConfigMgr server that hands out task sequences to clients (e.g. mp01.corp.local)\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Only when building a ConfigMgr bootable ISO - WinPE contacts this server to get the task sequence\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -DistributionPoint\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 The FQDN of the ConfigMgr server that stores OS images, drivers, and packages (e.g. dp01.corp.local)\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Only when building a ConfigMgr bootable ISO - WinPE downloads content from here\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SiteServer\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 The FQDN of the ConfigMgr site server, used as a fallback for PowerShell Remoting\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Only when building a ConfigMgr bootable ISO - fallback for PSRemoting\cell}\row
\pard\sa80\fs22 Key point: All of these are only needed in Build mode (when ConfigMgr creates the bootable ISO). If you're using -ExternalIsoPath to deploy a client-supplied ISO directly (which is the current design), none of these parameters are required - the ISO build/publish steps are skipped entirely.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 The documentation already notes this:\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2\cf2{\f1 ConfigMgr parameters (-SiteCode, -ManagementPoint, -DistributionPoint, -BootImageName, -TaskSequenceName, -SiteServer)\f0}\par}
\pard\sa80\fs22 : only needed in Build mode. When using {\f1 -ExternalIsoPath\f0}, these are not required because the ISO build/publish steps are skipped.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 Are these parameters something you use in your environment, or should they be removed/deprecated since you're deploying client-supplied ISOs directly?\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 \b Check with JS if these are required\b0\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 {\f1 -TaskSequenceName\f0} The name of the ConfigMgr "task sequence" - this is ConfigMgr's automation script that installs the OS, drivers, apps, etc. In the current code it's informational only - it's used to validate that the task sequence exists in ConfigMgr, but doesn't drive the build when using External ISO mode. If you're not building ConfigMgr media, this isn't needed.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 {\f1 -Skip\f0} parameters (all optional, none required)\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 These are optional bypass switches for validation checks. They exist so you can skip checks you don't need or that are failing for known reasons:\par
\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Parameter\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 What it skips\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 \clcbpat3 \b \b0 Why you'd use it\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SkipPreBuild\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 All pre-build validation\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 When you've already validated and just want to re-run\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SkipOneView\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Server resolution via OneView\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 When you already know the iLO IP and don't need OneView\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SkipIlo\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 iLO credential check\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 When iLO creds are already verified\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SkipDpMp\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Management Point / Distribution Point reachability\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 Not needed for External ISO mode\cell}\row\trowd\trgaph60\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx3008\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx6016\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs\cellx9024{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 -SkipIsoUrl\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 ISO URL reachability check\cell}{\pard\fi0\li60\ri60\fs22\sa40\sb40 When running offline or ISO is already verified\cell}\row
\pard\sa80\fs22 None are required - they're all optional conveniences.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 {\f1 -Force\f0} Acknowledges the server is powered On. In the actual build command (Invoke-PhysicalServerBuild), this is required to reboot a running server. In Configure-PhysicalBuild it's informational only (that command never reboots anything).\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 {\f1 -Deploy\f0} Skips the interactive APPROVE prompt and immediately executes the build. Useful for automation/scripts where no human is present to type APPROVE. Alias: -Execute.\par
\pard\sa80\fs22 {\f1 -PassThru\f0} Returns the structured result object (hashtable) for scripting. By default, the command only prints a human-readable report. With {\f1 -PassThru\f0}, you can capture the result:\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2\cf2{\f1 $result = Configure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 ... -PassThru -Deployif (-not $result.Success) \{ Handle-Error \}\f0}\par}
\pard\sa80\fs22 Summary: None of these are required for normal operation. The typical usage is just:\par
{\pard\sa80\sb80\fs20\fi0\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw10\brdrb\brdrs\brdrw10\clcbpat2\cf2{\f1 Configure-PhysicalBuild -ServerIdentifier srv01 -OneViewHost oneview.corp.local ` -ExternalIsoPath '\\\\fileserver\\isos\\Win2025.iso' -GuardRail 'srv01'\f0}\par}
\pard\sa80\fs22 \b Then type APPROVE when prompted.\b0\par}